+# Adversarial Review — GDX-8 Roll History
+
+## High
+
+- None found.
+
+## Medium
+
+### [Pass 1] Persisted `player_id` uses the Discord account ID instead of the authenticated player record ID
+
+- **Severity**: Medium
+- **File:line**: `server/routes/roll-log.js:34`; `server/middleware/auth.js:64-72`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: In production, any authenticated player or ST posts a valid roll. `requireAuth` supplies `req.user.id` as the Discord user ID and supplies the Mongo player-record identity separately as `req.user.player_id`; it does not supply `req.user._id`. The route evaluates `req.user._id || req.user.id || ''` and therefore persists the Discord ID.
+- **Observable consequence**: `roll_log.player_id` cannot be joined to the app's player documents using the player collection `_id`, despite the field name and route comment presenting it as a player identity. Test mocks can conceal this by giving `req.user._id` a convenient value.
+- **Confidence**: High.
+
+### [Pass 1] Initial feed loading races live frames, causing rolls to disappear or appear twice
+
+- **Severity**: Medium
+- **File:line**: `public/js/admin/roll-feed.js:29-49`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: An ST opens Engine, `initRollFeed()` marks the module initialized and begins its GET, and a `roll_log` frame arrives around the request. If the frame arrives while GET is pending, `onRollLogged()` prepends it, after which the GET replaces all of `_feed`; if the request snapshot did not include the roll it disappears. If the GET completes with a recent roll and the corresponding WS frame arrives afterward, the frame is prepended to the same row already returned by GET.
+- **Observable consequence**: The live ST feed can temporarily omit a real roll or display it twice. There is no `_id` de-duplication or merge of the fetch result with frames received in flight.
+- **Confidence**: High.
+
+### [Pass 1] The boot-time TTL index creation is launched without `await`
+
+- **Severity**: Medium
+- **File:line**: `server/index.js:327`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: Server startup reaches the new `createIndex()` call while MongoDB is slow/unavailable, or an index named `gdx8_roll_log_ttl` already exists with conflicting options. The Mongo driver returns a promise, but the call is neither awaited nor caught.
+- **Observable consequence**: Startup can proceed before the retention index exists, and a rejection bypasses the surrounding async startup flow's normal sequencing/error handling as an unhandled promise rejection. An identically specified existing index is idempotent, but an option change or manually created same-name index produces `IndexOptionsConflict` with no local handling.
+- **Confidence**: High that the promise is unawaited; medium on the process-level result because that depends on the runtime's unhandled-rejection policy and surrounding startup code not yet permitted in this pass.
+
+### [Pass 1] The write schema accepts internally impossible roll summaries
+
+- **Severity**: Medium
+- **File:line**: `server/schemas/roll_log.schema.js:19-29`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: A player posts for their own character with `successes: -50`, `results: []`, or extremely long `label`/`pool` strings. The schema bounds each supplied die to 1-10 and rejects unknown/missing fields, but puts no minimum on `successes`, no `minItems` on `results`, and no `maxLength` on client-controlled strings.
+- **Observable consequence**: Invalid or oversized records are accepted, persisted for 30 days, broadcast to every connected client, and rendered in the ST feed. This permits feed/data corruption and avoidable storage/frame amplification by any authenticated character owner.
+- **Confidence**: High.
+
+## Low
+
+### [Pass 1] Roll-log delivery failures are permanently silent
+
+- **Severity**: Low
+- **File:line**: `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:1087-1089`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: Every roll-log POST that fails because of a route-mount error, authorization regression, schema mismatch, network outage, or server error reaches `.catch(() => {})`.
+- **Observable consequence**: The player flow correctly remains non-blocking, but neither the player nor browser diagnostics receive any indication; a broken logging path can silently drop all rolls indefinitely and deprive operators of a useful signal.
+- **Confidence**: High.
+
+### [Pass 1] The renamed dice-engine regression assertion does not prove its stated invariant
+
+- **Severity**: Low
+- **File:line**: `server/tests/rlv-6-dice-engine-removed.test.js:46-48`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: Deleted wiring returns via a default import, an aliased named import such as `import { initDiceEngine as initEngine }`, a dynamic `import('./admin/dice-engine.js')`, or a re-export/alternate relative spelling.
+- **Observable consequence**: The test titled “never re-wires the deleted dice-engine.js” remains green although the removed module has been wired back in. Its regular expressions cover only one exact named-import shape, one exact source spelling, and direct calls under the original identifier.
+- **Confidence**: High for the assertion gap; low-to-medium likelihood of those alternative import shapes being used accidentally.
+

