    1: # Story gdx.8: persisted roll history + live ST roll feed
    2: 
    3: Status: review
    4: 
    5: ## Story
    6: 
    7: As a Storyteller running a live Terra Mortis session,
    8: I want every player roll made during the game to persist server-side and appear in a live feed I can
    9: watch in the admin app,
   10: so that I can follow the table's dice without asking players to read results aloud, and have a durable
   11: record afterward — without practice/prep rolls made outside a live session cluttering that record.
   12: 
   13: ## Why this story exists
   14: 
   15: GDX-7 (done) proved the `game_in_progress` flag and the roll-spend chain both work end to end. GDX-8
   16: is the next slice in the same sequencing (`986 ∥ 987 → 988 → 989`, GitHub #981): a new `roll_log`
   17: collection, gated the same way GDX-7 gates spend-on-roll, broadcasting to an admin feed the same way
   18: GDX-5 broadcasts settings changes. Depends on GDX-5 (`game_in_progress` flag + WS pattern) and GDX-7
   19: (the spend fields this story also records) — both done.
   20: 
   21: ## What this story is NOT
   22: 
   23: - NOT a change to `state.hist`/`addHist()`/`renderHist()` — the existing in-memory, 20-item-capped,
   24:   session-local roll history list (`public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:1030-1055`, rendered into `#hlist`).
   25:   That stays exactly as it is: a cosmetic, ephemeral, per-tab convenience. This story ADDS a parallel,
   26:   server-persisted write alongside it — same three call sites, genuinely new data path, not a
   27:   replacement.
   28: - NOT `roll.js` (legacy v1 roller). Scoped to `roll-v2.js` only, same boundary GDX-7 already
   29:   established for this whole epic. Do not touch `roll.js`.
   30: - NOT a change to GDX-7's own spend mechanism (`_currentSpendDecision`, `trackerAdj` calls). This
   31:   story only READS the already-computed `spend` object in `doRoll()` to record what was spent — it
   32:   does not alter when or how much is spent.
   33: - NOT reviving `public/js/admin/session-log.js`. That file is a **different, already-dead feature**
   34:   (free-text session-log entries, not roll history) whose own `initSessionLog` export is imported in
   35:   `admin.js` but never called anywhere — confirmed by grep, a real pre-existing gap left behind when
   36:   the old Engine domain's sibling tools (dice-engine.js, feeding-engine.js, session-tracker.js) were
   37:   deleted in rlv.6/#836 but this one import survived uncalled. This story's own new "Engine" sidebar
   38:   entry is a **new, purpose-built domain for roll history only** — it happens to reuse the same
   39:   domain name/id the old (fully removed) tools used, which is a coincidence of naming, not a revival.
   40:   Flag `session-log.js`'s own dead-code status in Completion Notes; do not silently wire it up or
   41:   delete it as part of this story — that is a separate, undiscussed decision for Angelus.
   42: - NOT initiative, frenzy, lashing-out, damage, reliquaries, blood fruits, or Influence spends — same
   43:   exclusions GDX-7 already established from the 25 Jul meeting decision, unrelated to this story's own
   44:   scope but worth restating since this story also touches `doRoll()`.
   45: - NOT a player-facing read surface. `GET /api/roll_log` is ST/dev only in this story — nothing in the
   46:   epic's own issue text, GDX-5, or GDX-7 asks for a player-visible roll history beyond the existing
   47:   client-local `#hlist`. A future story could add one; this one does not.
   48: - NOT retention/cleanup tooling beyond the TTL index itself (AC2). No admin UI to manually purge, no
   49:   export. If the feed grows unwieldy in practice, that is a future story's problem.
   50: 
   51: ## Acceptance Criteria
   52: 
   53: 1. **New `roll_log` collection**, one document per completed roll (chance die, standard, or
   54:    contested — all three of `doRoll()`'s existing result branches), written ONLY while
   55:    `getGlobalSettings()?.game_in_progress` is `true`. Shape:
   56:    ```
   57:    {
   58:      character_id, player_id, label, pool, results: [...],
   59:      successes, again_rule, rote, wp_bonus,
   60:      vitae_spent, wp_spent, rolled_at
   61:    }
   62:    ```
   63:    `player_id` is **server-derived from `req.user`**, never client-supplied — mirrors
   64:    `downtime.js:613`'s own `String(req.user._id || req.user.id || '')` pattern. `character_id` is
   65:    validated against `req.user.character_ids` (see AC5). `rolled_at` is a **genuine BSON `Date`**,
   66:    not `new Date().toISOString()` — see AC2's own TTL note for why this matters.
   67: 2. **TTL index, 30-day retention**, mirroring `server/index.js`'s own `crd1_terminal_status_ttl`
   68:    index exactly (same file, same `start()` block, `background: true`, `expireAfterSeconds: 2592000`).
   69:    **This collection must NOT repeat that index's own documented known limitation**: MongoDB's TTL
   70:    monitor only expires documents whose indexed field holds a real BSON `Date`, and
   71:    `contested_roll_requests`' own `updated_at` is a string, so that index is silently inert today
   72:    (`server/index.js:300-308`'s own comment names this explicitly). `roll_log.rolled_at` must be
   73:    written as a real `Date` object specifically so this collection's TTL index actually reaps
   74:    documents, unlike the precedent it otherwise mirrors.
   75: 3. **`POST /api/roll_log`** — new route, `requireAuth` only at mount (matches `contested-rolls.js`'s
   76:    own mount shape), scoped so a player can only log a roll for a character in their own
   77:    `req.user.character_ids` (ST/dev unconditional, mirroring `tracker.js`'s `canAccess()` shape).
   78:    Returns 201 with the written doc (or its `_id`) on success.
   79: 4. **`GET /api/roll_log`** — ST/dev only (`requireRole('st')` or equivalent role check, matching this
   80:    project's established ST-gated read pattern e.g. `office_actions`). Returns the most recent N
   81:    entries (reasonable default, e.g. 50) sorted `rolled_at` descending, for the admin feed's initial
   82:    paint before the WS stream takes over.
   83: 5. **`broadcastRollLogged(doc)`** in `server/ws.js`, mirroring `broadcastCatalogueUpdate`'s exact
   84:    shape (`_fanOut(JSON.stringify({...}))`, not raw client iteration — the post-ADMR-1 established
   85:    pattern). Frame shape: `{ type: 'roll_log', ...doc }` (send the whole small doc, not just an id —
   86:    the admin feed renders directly from the frame without a second fetch, since this is a
   87:    high-frequency event during a live session and a round-trip-per-roll would be wasteful). Called
   88:    from the `POST` route after a successful write.
   89: 6. **Client (player side): hook into all three of `doRoll()`'s existing `addHist(...)` call sites**
   90:    (`public/js/suite/roll-v2.js` lines ~919, ~990, ~1020 as of this story's own read — re-verify at
   91:    dev-story time) — alongside each `addHist(...)` call, when `getGlobalSettings()?.game_in_progress`
   92:    is `true` AND `state.rollChar` is set, fire a `POST /api/roll_log` with the fields AC1 lists,
   93:    gathered from what's already in scope at that point in `doRoll()`: `state.rollChar._id`
   94:    (character_id), the branch's own `pool`/`lbl`/`cnt` values (label/pool/successes — reuse exactly
   95:    what's already being passed to `addHist`, not a second computation), the raw dice array (`cA`/`cB`
   96:    as applicable to the branch), `state.AGAIN` (again_rule), `state.ROTE` (rote), `state.WP`
   97:    (wp_bonus), and the `spend.cost.vitaeCost`/`spend.cost.willpowerCost` values already computed
   98:    earlier in the same `doRoll()` call (GDX-7's own spend decision — read them, do not recompute).
   99:    Fire-and-forget (mirrors `trackerAdj`'s own established fire-and-forget shape; do not block the
  100:    roll UI on this write's own round-trip). When the flag is OFF, this story adds **zero** new
  101:    behaviour — `addHist()` and everything else in `doRoll()` are byte-for-byte unchanged.
  102: 7. **Client (admin side): live roll feed panel** in a new "Engine" sidebar domain (see Dev Notes —
  103:    Domain Placement for why this is a NEW addition, not a revival of anything). On domain open: `GET
  104:    /api/roll_log` for the initial list. While open (or globally, matching this project's existing
  105:    `initWS({...})` pattern — confirm at dev-story time whether admin's WS connection is domain-scoped
  106:    or global): a new `onRollLogged` callback wired into `admin.js`'s own `initWS({...})` call,
  107:    prepending each new frame to the feed live, capped at a reasonable display length (e.g. 50,
  108:    mirroring `state.hist`'s own 20-cap precedent, exact number is a UI judgement call for dev-story).
  109: 8. **`game_in_progress` `false` = nothing persists, byte-for-byte unchanged client roll flow.** Every
  110:    piece of AC6 is gated behind the same single flag read GDX-7 already established as the pattern.
  111:    Practice/prep rolls made with the flag off never reach `roll_log` at all — not even a rejected
  112:    write, no POST is attempted.
  113: 9. Real test coverage: server-side auth-boundary tests (player can POST their own character's roll;
  114:    player 403/blocked posting another character's roll or reading `GET /api/roll_log` at all; ST/dev
  115:    can do both), the TTL index's own `Date`-not-string proof (mirroring
  116:    `crd-1-contested-roll-request-shape.test.js`'s own TTL-shape test), the `broadcastRollLogged` WS
  117:    emission (mirroring `stm-9-ws-broadcast.test.js`'s `vi.spyOn` pattern), and pure-function unit
  118:    tests for whatever client-side field-gathering logic gets extracted (mirrors gdx-7's own
  119:    "extract pure decision functions rather than leaving them inline" convention). A documented manual
  120:    browser-smoke step for the one thing genuinely hard to unit test end to end (a live roll appearing
  121:    in a second, admin-side browser tab without a refresh).
